  "notes": "Issue #459. Model diversity arm parallel to EXP-449 (LightGBM) and #457 (stacking), built on top of EXP-374 (currently valid legacy parent while N5/parser-native baseline reset is still in progress per roadmap #422). Feature set is EXP-374's build_fold_features() reused unchanged (parser v2.1.0 stop-notation-invariant + Ensembl isoform mask + pathway families + hotspot-34). Only the model changes, from XGBoost to CatBoost. Starting hyperparameters are EXP-127's GPU CatBoost config (iterations=1000, depth=8, learning_rate=0.05, l2_leaf_reg=3, border_count=32, bootstrap_type=Bernoulli, subsample=0.8), reduced to a CPU-feasible depth=6/iterations=400/rsm=0.1 based on the preflight timing above -- this is a compute-bounded config, not a retuned one, so results are not a like-for-like comparison against EXP-127's GPU run. No Optuna, no retuning beyond the compute-forced reduction. Target, test distribution and Public LB do not define any parameter here."
